				<div class="post-721 post hentry category-virtual-pc">
			<h2 id="post-721"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2008/08/reason-29-for-using-virtual-machines/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Reason #29 for using Virtual Machines">Reason #29 for using Virtual Machines</a></h2>
			<small class="meta">August 6th, 2008 </small>

			<div class="entry">
				<p>Today I blew up a server.&nbsp; Couldn&#8217;t figure something out so I pushed every button I could find, flipped every switch and changed every setting.&nbsp; Nothing.&nbsp; So you know what I did, I deleted it, copied over a new <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/06/13/sysprep-your-virtual-pc-images.aspx" target="_blank">Sysprepped Hard Drive</a> and had a clean slate in about 5 minutes.</p>
<p>I figured out my problem, by the way.</p>
